trajectory.patch:
Based on my analysis of the provided source code and the context of USB Audio Class 2, the issue lies in the device tree overlays for samples that use `sof-synchronized` clocks. These configurations intend to create synchronous audio endpoints to avoid using feedback mechanisms. However, the devicetree macros for UAC2 default to creating asynchronous endpoints with explicit feedback for OUT interfaces if no feedback type is specified. This contradicts the intention of using a `sof-synchronized` clock.

The fix is to add a `synchronous;` property to the `zephyr,uac2-audio-streaming` nodes that are associated with a `sof-synchronized` clock. This property will instruct the descriptor generation macros to create a synchronous endpoint without any feedback mechanism, aligning the implementation with the design goal.

Here are the required changes:

samples/bluetooth/audio/bap_broadcast_sink/app.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
		as_iso_in: in_interface {
			compatible = "zephyr,uac2-audio-streaming";
			linked-terminal = <&in_terminal>;
			subslot-size = <2>;
			bit-resolution = <16>;
		};
========
		as_iso_in: in_interface {
			compatible = "zephyr,uac2-audio-streaming";
			linked-terminal = <&in_terminal>;
			synchronous;
			subslot-size = <2>;
			bit-resolution = <16>;
		};
>>>>>>>> REPLACE

